    "body": "\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n\r\nFix the `store_threshold` and `max_tracker_size` descriptions in `docs/features/kv_offloading_usage.md`: the threshold counts store offers, not lookups. The behavior was changed in https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/52227.\r\n\r\n## Claims\r\n\r\n- `store_threshold` and `max_tracker_size` descriptions match `CPUOffloadingManager` behavior.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\nDocs-only change, checked against the code:\r\n\r\n- `CPUOffloadingManager.prepare_store()` (`vllm/v1/kv_offload/cpu/manager.py`) records accesses and filters store candidates by `store_threshold`; `lookup()` does not update the counts.\r\n- The existing `test_filter_reused_manager` (`tests/v1/kv_offload/cpu/test_manager.py`) asserts that `lookup()` does not count towards store admission.\r\n\r\nDocs build:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nAPI_AUTONAV_EXCLUDE=vllm mkdocs build\r\n```\r\n\r\nBuild succeeds; the updated rows render correctly in `features/kv_offloading_usage/`.\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n\r\nThe previous \"lookups\" wording was incorrect.\r\n\r\nNot a duplicate: no open PR changes these descriptions (`gh pr list --repo vllm-project/vllm --state open --search \"store_threshold\"`).\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\r\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\r\n\r\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\r\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\r\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\r\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n<a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/vllm-project/codesmith/vllm/pr/63686?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-light-v3.svg\"><img alt=\"View with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3-3x.png\" width=\"162\" height=\"28\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1795589894&installation_model_id=425286&pr_number=63686&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=vllm-project%2Fvllm&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fvllm-project%2Fvllm%2Fpull%2F63686&signature=60b125bf965f8d8c0621a90975ab9ae6e1406e2200e15b1db5b24de396936de6\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\r\n<sup>Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\r\n\r\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\r\n---\r\n<a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/vllm-project/codesmith/vllm/pr/63686?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.s